@* A Mermaid diagram someone is writing (a .mmd file, a ```mermaid block of a Markdown file), drawn by the Mermaid the
   app bundles (interop/mermaid.js draw: "strict" security). A mistake never blanks it: the last good drawing stays,
   and Mermaid's own message is shown with the line it points at (told on, so the source can mark the line). *@
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime Js
@inject ThemeState Theme

<div class="wb-diagram" data-drawn="@(_drawnOnce ? "true" : "false")" data-error-line="@(_error?.Line)">
    @if (_error is { } error)
    {
        <div class="wb-preview-error" role="alert">
            <strong>@(error.Line > 0 ? $"Line {error.Line}: the diagram cannot be drawn." : "The diagram cannot be drawn.")</strong>
            <pre class="wb-preview-error-words">@error.Message</pre>
        </div>
    }
    <div class="mermaid-host wb-diagram-host" @ref="_host" role="img" aria-label="Diagram"></div>
</div>

@code {
    private ElementReference _host;
    private IJSObjectReference? _module;
    private string? _drawn;
    private bool _drawnOnce;
    private DiagramProblem? _error;

    /// <summary>The diagram's Mermaid text.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Text { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Drawn, or not: the problem (null: drawn) for the source's line mark.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<DiagramProblem?> OnProblem { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Drawn at least once, and its text as it is now has no mistake.</summary>
    public bool Drawn => _drawnOnce && _error is null && _drawn is not null;

    /// <summary>Where the diagram is drawn (its SVG): for its picture.</summary>
    public ElementReference Host => _host;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => Theme.Changed += Redraw;

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        var wanted = $"{Theme.Effective}\n{Text}";
        if (wanted == _drawn)
        {
            return;
        }
        _drawn = wanted;
        DiagramProblem? found = null;
        if (Text.Trim().Length > 0)
        {
            _module ??= await Js.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./js/mermaid.js");
            found = await _module.InvokeAsync<DiagramProblem?>("draw", _host, Text);
            _drawnOnce = _drawnOnce || found is null;
        }
        if (found != _error)
        {
            _error = found;
            await OnProblem.InvokeAsync(found);
        }
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    private void Redraw() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        Theme.Changed -= Redraw;
        if (_module is not null)
        {
            try
            {
                await _module.DisposeAsync();
            }
            catch (JSDisconnectedException)
            {
                // the page is going
            }
        }
    }
}
